---
// The blog's masthead ground: the home page's nebula still, recolored with
// the worn theme the same way an author's portrait is (Portrait.astro). The
// still keeps its own light and shape, the accent lends it a hue, and it
// fades out into the page before the reading starts. Decoration only, so it
// is hidden from assistive tech and holds no content.
//
// It is the hero's still (assets-static/nebula-still-*.jpg), already cached by
// anyone who came from the home page; no new image.
---

<div class="sky" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
  .sky {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto;
    height: min(34rem, 80svh);
    overflow: hidden;
    isolation: isolate;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: url('/assets/nebula-still-dark.jpg') center 30% / cover no-repeat var(--bg-deep);
    --sky-tint: 0.6;
    --sky-strength: 0.7;
    opacity: var(--sky-strength);
    /* fades to nothing well above the fold's end, so no line of body text
       ever sits on the picture */
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 0%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55) 45%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .sky::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: var(--accent-primary);
    mix-blend-mode: color;
    opacity: var(--sky-tint);
  }

  :global([data-theme='light']) .sky {
    background-image: url('/assets/nebula-still-light.jpg');
    --sky-tint: 0.35;
    --sky-strength: 0.55;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :global([data-theme='auto']) .sky {
      background-image: url('/assets/nebula-still-light.jpg');
      --sky-tint: 0.35;
      --sky-strength: 0.55;
    }
  }
</style>
